### Transcendence Backend API
### Use with the "REST Client" VSCode extension.
### Run requests top to bottom for a normal flow (register -> login -> me -> refresh -> logout).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:9000
@email = user@email.com
@password = password

### =========================================================
### Health
### =========================================================

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health


### =========================================================
### Auth  (/api/auth)
### =========================================================

### Register a new user
# role must be "artist" or "hirer"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "name": "Test User",
  "role": "artist"
}


### Login
# Sets refreshToken cookie automatically (handled by REST Client cookie jar)
# Captures the access token into {{login.response.body.token}} for later requests
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Get current user (from token payload)
# Requires Authorization header with the access token returned by /login
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### Refresh access token
# Uses the refreshToken cookie set by /login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh


### Logout
# Uses the refreshToken cookie set by /login, clears it
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout


### =========================================================
### Users  (/api/users)
### =========================================================

### Get my profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}


### List all users (admin only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
